{%- comment -%}
  PG Cart Timer: a 10-minute "extra 5% off" window that starts when the shopper
  first has something in the cart, shown at the bottom of the cart drawer and
  applied to their order automatically.

  THE OFFER IS REAL, AND SO IS THE CLOCK. The discount is a genuine Shopify code
  (RUSH5, 5% off all items, combines with product discounts so it stacks on top
  of the Buy 2 Get 1 bundle rather than replacing it). Two deliberate choices
  keep the countdown honest rather than theatrical:

    - The deadline is stored in localStorage, so it SURVIVES reloads and
      navigation. A timer that restarts at 10:00 on every page view would be
      telling the shopper something untrue.
    - When it reaches zero the offer really stops: the block disappears and
      checkout stops routing through the discount.

  WHEN IT STARTS AND RESTARTS. The window opens the first time the cart is seen
  non-empty, and opens again on any genuine ADD -- whenever the item count goes
  UP. It is cleared when the cart is emptied.

  It deliberately does NOT restart on a page view. That distinction is the whole
  point: reopening the offer because someone reloaded would make the countdown a
  prop, while reopening it when they actually add something is true -- the ten
  minutes really do start from that add. The previous count is kept in
  localStorage so navigating between pages is not mistaken for an add.

  The consequence is intended: if the window runs out and the shopper adds
  nothing further, the offer is over and the block disappears rather than
  quietly resurrecting itself.

  WHERE IT SITS. As the first child of .sticky-in-panel -- the pinned pane that
  carries Shipping Protection, the total and CHECKOUT -- so it is the last thing
  read before the button, which is the point of it.

  It is NOT inserted directly before that pane, even though that is nearer the
  literal "bottom of the cart". Two things already compete for that exact slot:
  pg-cart-mobile's placeUnlock (the upsell) and its placeSpacer (the flex spacer
  that pins the pane down on a short cart), each of which re-inserts itself
  immediately before the pane on every apply() pass. Adding a third element to
  that fight is how rows start swapping places. Inside the pane there is no
  contention at all.

  HOW THE DISCOUNT IS APPLIED. Clicking CHECKOUT while the window is open goes
  to /discount/RUSH5?redirect=/checkout -- Shopify's own endpoint, which records
  the code against the session and forwards to checkout, so the saving is already
  on the order summary when the page opens. Nothing is typed and nothing is
  stored in the cart, so an expired window simply stops redirecting and the next
  click is an ordinary checkout. The interception is wrapped in try/catch and is
  skipped entirely unless the window is open: if anything at all goes wrong here,
  the click falls through to the theme's normal checkout.

  THE CART ITSELF IS LEFT ALONE, by request. The block says APPLIED IN CART --
  the shopper does not have to type a code or hunt for a field, the 5% is on
  their order automatically -- but no line, total or saving figure in the drawer
  is rewritten by this section. The only number that moves is the one Shopify
  itself computes once the code is recorded.

  window.pgRush is exposed so pg-cart-sticky can show the same countdown in the
  product-page bar without a second clock that could drift out of step.

  ================================================================
  IT ALSO CARRIES THE RECOMMENDATION HIDE, for a platform reason rather than a
  design one: Shopify caps a section group at 25 sections and overlay-group was
  already full, so this could not ship as a 26th entry. The two rules below used
  to be their own pg-cart-declutter section; they are cart-drawer styling like
  everything else here, so this is where they went.

  They hide nc-recs' two optional add-to-cart blocks -- .nc-recs ("You may also
  like", under the item list) and .nc-recs-panel ("Add & save more", inside the
  checkout panel) -- which pushed the order total down and made the cart read as
  a catalogue. The pg-unlock offer rows are untouched. Only these two blocks are
  hidden rather than the nc-recs section removed, because that same file supplies
  most of the drawer's styling: the compact top, the 120px thumbnails, the
  bundle-savings progress bar, the slim shipping bar and the quantity stepper.
  CSS rather than deleting the nodes, since nc-recs.js re-injects them whenever
  the cart changes.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  /* the optional "recommended purchase" rows -- see the note above */
  #cart .nc-recs,
  #cart .nc-recs-panel{display:none !important}

  #pg-rush{
    display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:8px;
    margin:0 0 6px;padding:7px 10px;
    border-radius:10px;
    background:linear-gradient(120deg,rgba(139,68,190,.16),rgba(199,155,234,.12));
    border:1px solid rgba(168,120,214,.42);
    font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:800;
    text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.03em;
    color:#3B2352;
    text-align:center;
  }
  #pg-rush .pg-rush-c{
    font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;
    font-weight:800;
    background:#8B44BE;color:#fff;
    padding:3px 7px;border-radius:6px;
    letter-spacing:.02em;
  }
  #pg-rush .pg-rush-x{color:#6B3E93}
  @media (max-width:760px){
    #pg-rush{font-size:10.5px;padding:6px 8px;margin-bottom:5px;letter-spacing:.02em}
  }
</style>
<script>
(function(){
  if (window.pgRush) return;

  var KEY = 'pgRushEnds', WINDOW_MS = 10 * 60 * 1000, CODE = 'RUSH5';

  function read(){
    try { return parseInt(localStorage.getItem(KEY), 10) || 0; } catch(e){ return 0; }
  }
  function write(v){ try { localStorage.setItem(KEY, String(v)); } catch(e){} }
  function drop(){ try { localStorage.removeItem(KEY); } catch(e){} }

  function left(){
    var end = read();
    if (!end) return 0;
    return Math.max(0, end - Date.now());
  }
  function active(){ return left() > 0; }
  function fmt(){
    var s = Math.ceil(left() / 1000);
    var m = Math.floor(s / 60);
    var r = s % 60;
    return m + ':' + (r < 10 ? '0' : '') + r;
  }

  window.pgRush = {left: left, active: active, fmt: fmt, code: CODE};

  /* Start on the first non-empty cart; restart on a real ADD (count goes up);
     clear when the cart empties. The previous count is persisted so that moving
     between pages is not read as an add. */
  var CKEY = 'pgRushCount';
  function lastCount(){
    try { var v = localStorage.getItem(CKEY); return v === null ? -1 : (parseInt(v, 10) || 0); }
    catch(e){ return -1; }
  }
  function keepCount(n){ try { localStorage.setItem(CKEY, String(n)); } catch(e){} }

  function onCount(n){
    var prev = lastCount();
    keepCount(n);
    if (n === 0){ drop(); return; }
    if (prev >= 0 && n > prev){ write(Date.now() + WINDOW_MS); return; }  /* a real add */
    if (!read()) write(Date.now() + WINDOW_MS);                          /* first sighting */
  }

  var busy = false;
  function poll(){
    if (busy) return;
    busy = true;
    fetch('/cart.js', {headers: {'Accept': 'application/json'}, credentials: 'same-origin'})
      .then(function(r){ return r.ok ? r.json() : null; })
      .then(function(j){
        if (j && typeof j.item_count === 'number') onCount(j.item_count);
        busy = false; render();
      })
      .catch(function(){ busy = false; });
  }

  function render(){
    var pane = document.querySelector('#cart .sticky-in-panel');
    var el = document.getElementById('pg-rush');
    if (!active()){
      if (el && el.parentNode) el.parentNode.removeChild(el);
      return;
    }
    if (!pane) return;
    if (!el){
      el = document.createElement('div');
      el.id = 'pg-rush';
      el.innerHTML = '<span class="pg-rush-c">0:00</span>' +
                     '<span class="pg-rush-x">EXTRA <b>5% OFF</b> ENTIRE ORDER &mdash; APPLIED IN CART</span>';
    }
    if (pane.firstChild !== el) pane.insertBefore(el, pane.firstChild);
    var c = el.querySelector('.pg-rush-c');
    var t = fmt();
    if (c && c.textContent !== t) c.textContent = t;
  }

  /* CHECKOUT -> apply the code first, then go to checkout */
  document.addEventListener('click', function(e){
    try {
      if (!e.target.closest) return;
      var btn = e.target.closest('button[name="checkout"], input[name="checkout"], [data-pg-checkout]');
      if (!btn) return;
      if (!active()) return;                 /* window closed: ordinary checkout */
      e.preventDefault();
      e.stopImmediatePropagation();
      window.location.href = '/discount/' + CODE + '?redirect=%2Fcheckout';
    } catch(err){ /* never block checkout */ }
  }, true);

  function boot(){
    poll();
    setInterval(render, 1000);

    /* the drawer is rebuilt on every add, remove and quantity change */
    if (window.MutationObserver){
      var drawer = document.getElementById('cart');
      if (drawer){
        var queued = false;
        new MutationObserver(function(){
          if (queued) return;
          queued = true;
          setTimeout(function(){ queued = false; poll(); }, 250);
        }).observe(drawer, {childList: true, subtree: true});
      }
    }
    document.addEventListener('click', function(e){
      if (!e.target.closest) return;
      if (e.target.closest('[name="add"], .pgx-atc, #pg-sticky, .pg-unlock-go, form[action*="/cart/add"] button')){
        setTimeout(poll, 600); setTimeout(poll, 1800);
      }
    }, true);
    [900, 2600].forEach(function(t){ setTimeout(poll, t); });
  }

  if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', boot);
  else boot();
})();
</script>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Cart Timer", "settings": [], "presets": [{"name": "PG Cart Timer"}]}
{% endschema %}
